    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d429">

                <pb facs="0626" n="2090" sameAs="frus:frus1951v06p2/pg2090"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">891.03/1–2451: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            Embassy in India
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1951-01-24T20:00:00-05:00">January 24, 1951—8
                            p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1147. Urgently need all available convincing material re humanitarian side
                    probable effects India food emergency for possible presentation Cong. Pls
                    airmail priority any graphic material distressed areas present or past including
                    revealing photographs, etc. Also need Emb best estimates probable deaths, other
                    suffering, reduced natl and local caloric intake, short-run and long-run
                    effects, if emergency requirement not met. Psychological and polit effects. Some
                    indication localization effects food deficiency.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
